  "bodyText": "Home\nVisit Us\nExhibitions\nEvents\nOnline Talks\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nCollections\nBlog\nResearch\nLearning\nShop\nCart\nMy Account\nAbout\nBecome a Friend\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\n\n01993 810 210\n\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\n  \nHome\nEvents\nExhibitions\nCollections\nFriends’ Membership\nVisit\nShop\nBasket\nMy Account\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nResearch\nLearning\nOnline Talks\nBlog\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\nImage Services\nAbout\nBooks\nGifts\nThe Oxfordshire and Buckinghamshire Light Infantry Chronicle 1944-45\n£40.00\n\nSorry, this item is out of stock\n\nWartime chronicle covering the movements and actions of each of the Oxfordshire & Buckinghamshire Light Infantry's battalions during the years 1944-45. Includes maps and photographs.\n\nPlease Note: All Hardback, original, ex-library copies supplied. All in used but reasonable condition. Copy supplied may vary slightly from the one pictured in terms of wear and aging.\n\n \n\nRelated products\nBugle & Sabre I\n£5.00 Add to cart\nChildren and War – A Bugle & Sabre Special\n£2.00 Add to cart\nBugle & Sabre II\n£5.00 Add to cart\nA True Soldier Gentleman: The Memoirs of Lt. John Cooke 1791-1813\n£3.95 Add to cart\n\nSoldiers of Oxfordshire Museum\nPark Street.\nWoodstock\nOxfordshire OX20 1SN\n\nPhone and Email:\nGeneral Enquiries & Event Tickets: 01993 810 211\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\nPrivacy Policy\nTerms and conditions",
